{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1527480-influence-v-arcana","id":1527480,"title":"Influence v. Arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-26T21:03:14-08:00","id":1527480,"title":"Influence v. Arcana","content":"How do you view influence as opposed to arcana? As an example is death influence roughly comparable the death arcana? Which do you view as broader in scope? Stronger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T01:15:36-08:00","id":1527485,"title":"","content":"Influences get Strengthen at 1 dot; much earlier than its Arcana counterpart, Perfecting. That's a sure advantage.<br /> <br /> I also feel Influences should have much more 'narrative permission' within their domains than corresponding spells, though I can't think of a nice example atm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Note the comparison to <i>spells</i>, though. Not Arcana. A dot in an Arcanum is way much broader in scope.<br /> <br /> Of course, certain Influences do better than others, like the given Death Influence... but while Control Death could allow a spirit to temporarily halt or even rewind medical deaths like a Master of Death can, a 'mere' Disciple of Death can conjure frost and summon ghosts and raise zombies and rip away souls, so yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T04:32:37-08:00","id":1527490,"title":"","content":"I would say the Arcana are much, much wider in scope. Death gives you control over things like shadows, entropy, ghosts, Twilight, souls (to an extent) etc.<br /> Someone with Influence Death doesn't get any of that. It's just the dying/being dead parts that matter.<br /> <br /> Arcana also have much more control over spell factors, like duration and scale, where Influences have their duration dependent on their total dot rating and only Mass Create explicitly allows multiple targets (though size of AoE effects are just ST fiat when it comes to Influences).<br /> <br /> As mentioned, Influences have different effects at different dot rankings (like Strengthen vs Perfection above, and Create being at 4 dots instead of Making at 5).<br /> <br /> Lastly, spells have well defined bounds for what all the practices can do, not just in types of effects but how those effects can work within the rules. Influences has the former (what type of effect each dot rating has should be obvious in most cases) but not the latter (how to express those effects) other than for Manifestation Conditions. In a way it's a type of narrative freedom, but for me it's the absolutely weakest point of the Influence system. STs just don't get enough guidelines to know how to use them. It gets better once you have a good sense for how various things should be expressed in the rules framework, but that doesn't help new STs picking up CofD/GMC, Demon, Geist or Werewolf, where ephemeral entities are a core part of the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T07:04:18-08:00","id":1527492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1527480-influence-v-arcana#post1527480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you view influence as opposed to arcana? As an example is death influence roughly comparable the death arcana? Which do you view as broader in scope? Stronger?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the difference between &quot;narrow focus with greater power&quot; (Influence) versus &quot;broad capabilites with incremental power&quot; (Arcana).<br /> <br /> A starting dot in Influence is more potent that a starting dot in Arcana, but only in the narrow scope of the Influence; meanwhile the Arcana can do vastly more things with a single dot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T07:56:30-08:00","id":1527496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1527480-influence-v-arcana?p=1527485#post1527485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Influences get Strengthen at 1 dot; much earlier than its Arcana counterpart, Perfecting. That's a sure advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Strengthen Influence and Perfecting Practice are thoroughly comparable. Perfecting can improve things along more abstract lines, or with more multiplicative enhancements, whereas Strengthen is a bit more linear and, when expressed in mechanical terms, tends to provide a bonus limited to the spirit's Rank.<br /> <br /> I'm also not inclined to think that Control can direct a subject much more than a Ruling spell could.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T09:19:52-08:00","id":1527501,"title":"","content":"I think of Influence as direct control over its portfolio, such that using it is like moving an arm. Arcana I think is more like a collected body of mystic knowledge that a mage still needs to actually cast the right spell to take advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}